{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Z2TFFgx9SKH1Fk6Vre3rJ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== git log for graph.py / routing.py / unit_graph.py / workbook.py ===\nd27b7dc plans+runtime: plan 26 P-N20-002/P-N32-002 patch rounds, graph topology fix, N90 audit attempt, refreshed receipts\n165555d plans+runtime: plan 26 N31 repair/acceptance fixes, N32 patch round, reverified receipts and logs\n691e176 runtime+plans: plan 26 N31-N40 (repair acceptance, workbook terminals, CLI cutover) with receipts and evidence\n7fbb202 runtime+plans: plan 26 v3 (graph, qa criteria, prompt graph controller), langgraph_factory node/transport fixes, unit_content schema, refreshed evidence\nd5149bb runtime+plans: plan 26 v2 (schema, prompts, qa criteria), langgraph_factory runtime, plan26 test suite, CI workflow\n\n=== P-N20-002 patch ===\nschema_version: 1\npatch_id: P-N20-002\naction: overlay\ngraph_id: plan26_langgraph_curriculum_factory_implementation\nbase_graph_digest: 18d619bb4eb509d1c6c590699ce2072660f36781c33cbc18a4ad1f9f8501cac7\ntarget_node: N20_GRAPH_COMPILER\nscope: node_only\nreason: 'P-N20-001''s own fix to test_an_unwired_undeclared_node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id\n  selects its victim node against the wide compiled topology but reproduces the error\n  against the narrow binding_inventory(), a mismatch that only surfaces now that N32''s\n  wiring (P-N32-001) is the last layer and nearly everything is compiled. Precisely\n  diagnosed: swap the repro call to use full_binding_inventory() too'\nexpected_effect: test_plan26_topology.py's full suite passes again, closing this residual\n  inconsistency\ninstructions: \"One small, precisely-diagnosed residual bug in your own P-N20-001 fix,\\\n  \\ now\\nthat N32's wiring (P-N32-001) is the last layer: `test_an_unwired_undeclared_\\n\\\n  node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id` (around line 320) computes its `candidates`\\n\\\n  list by comparing `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` against the WIDE compiled topology's\\n`wired_endpoints`\\\n  \\ (from the `compiled` fixture, built against `full_binding_\\ninventory()`), but\\\n  \\ then reproduces the expected error with:\\n\\n    G.register_skeleton(fresh_builder(),\\\n  \\ G.binding_inventory())\\n\\n\\u2014 the NARROW `binding_inventory()`. Since `binding_inventory()`\\\n  \\ never\\ncontains any of D16-D32 (by design), none of `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`'s keys\\n\\\n  (all D18-D23/D25-D32/M06-M08) are ever in `registered` for that narrower\\ncall,\\\n  \\ so `_validate_topology`'s per-node loop never reaches the popped key\\nat all \\u2014\\\n  \\ the call succeeds instead of raising, regardless of which\\n`DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`\\\n  \\ entry was popped. This mismatch (selecting the victim\\nagainst the wide set, reproducing\\\n  \\ against the narrow one) is what breaks:\\nverified directly \\u2014 `pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py::\\n\\\n  test_an_unwired_undeclared_node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id` fails with\\n\\\"DID\\\n  \\ NOT RAISE\\\" against the current repository state.\\n\\nFix: make the repro call\\\n  \\ consistent with how the victim was selected \\u2014 use\\n`G.full_binding_inventory()`\\\n  \\ for the `register_skeleton` call too (since\\n`candidates` is computed against\\\n  \\ what that same wide set actually wires).\\nDo not change how `candidates` is selected\\\n  \\ (that logic is already correct);\\nonly the call on the line that currently reads\\\n  \\ `G.register_skeleton(fresh_\\nbuilder(), G.binding_inventory())` needs `G.binding_inventory()`\\\n  \\ replaced\\nwith `G.full_binding_inventory()`.\\n\\nThis is the only change needed.\\\n  \\ Do not touch anything else in this file, and\\ndo not touch `graph.py`, `routing.py`,\\\n  \\ or any other file. Re-run this node's\\nfull required verification command\\n(`{python}\\\n  \\ -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py\\ntests/runtime/test_plan26_state_reducers.py\\n\\\n  tests/runtime/test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py\\ntests/runtime/test_plan26_model_nodes.py`)\\\n  \\ and confirm it is fully green\\nbefore reporting `status: PASSED` as a bare line.\\n\"\ncontext: {}\ncreated_at: '2026-08-13T00:01:04.955693+00:00'\n\n=== P-N32-002 patch ===\nschema_version: 1\npatch_id: P-N32-002\naction: overlay\ngraph_id: plan26_langgraph_curriculum_factory_implementation\nbase_graph_digest: 18d619bb4eb509d1c6c590699ce2072660f36781c33cbc18a4ad1f9f8501cac7\ntarget_node: N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\nscope: node_only\nreason: N32's own D24-D32 wiring (P-N32-001) causes 4 residual failures in test_plan26_unit_graph.py,\n  the same class of consequence N31 already diagnosed and closed for D16-D23 (P-N31-003).\n  One test's frontier assertion needs to become a positive UNIT_ACCEPTED check; three\n  share a helper that assumed a clean episode always halts at a deferred edge, no\n  longer true now that this is likely the last topology-wiring layer\nexpected_effect: 'test_plan26_unit_graph.py reaches full green, closing this recursive\n  cascade; N32 can then report a genuine bare status: PASSED'\ninstructions: \"`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` is now also in your write\\\n  \\ set,\\nspecifically for four residual failures your D24-D32 wiring (P-N32-001)\\n\\\n  causes \\u2014 the same class of consequence N31 already diagnosed and closed for\\n\\\n  its own D16-D23 wiring (P-N31-003), one layer further now that your own\\ncorrection\\\n  \\ is real too. This is very likely the last layer: no further\\nnode in this graph\\\n  \\ adds compiled-graph topology after N32. Fix exactly\\nthese, nothing else in that\\\n  \\ file:\\n\\n1. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`\\n\\\n  \\   \\u2014 its final assertion currently reads `assert state[\\\"terminal\\\"][\\\"kind\\\"\\\n  ]\\n   not in (\\\"UNIT_ACCEPTED\\\", \\\"COMPLETE\\\")`, written when D24 was still\\n  \\\n  \\ unreachable so the clean one-unit (\\\"mode\\\": \\\"one\\\") episode could never\\n  \\\n  \\ reach 