rsistence.py:1052-1071` (`classify_join_members`) explicitly rejects `extra` members outside the expected denominator (`raise PersistenceError(f\"completed members outside the denominator: {extra}\")`) and treats a join `satisfied` only when `pending` is empty — fails closed.\n\n**4. Repair — PASS**\n`repair.py:882-952` (`D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR`) recomputes the parent/child diff itself via `json_pointer_diff` (never trusting the model's own manifest), checks `declared_parent_sha == current_hash` (rejects stale parents as `SystemFailure`/\"integrity\"), and computes `out_of_bound = [... not within_boundary(...)]`, raising `SystemFailure` if any changed pointer falls outside the declared repair boundary (`repair.py:944-952`). This is a hard `require(...)` (fail closed), not a warning.\n\n**5. Persistence/resume — PASS**\n`persistence.py:538-545` builds the real `SqliteSaver` from `langgraph.checkpoint.sqlite`. `validate_resume_inputs` (`persistence.py:1011-1031`) walks every observed field, refusing resume (`ResumeRefused`) if the field is unclassified or its digest differs from the baseline, keyed by `_DRIFT_FIELD_CLASSES` (`persistence.py:992-1008`): identity, frozen_digest, executable, evidence, accepted_bytes. `_validate_terminal_legality` (`persistence.py:1034-1044`) refuses resume unless the prior terminal is in `RESUMABLE_TERMINALS`. `compute_resume_frontier` (`persistence.py:1074-1123`) rewrites any model-node destination to the classification entry rather than replaying it directly, preventing replay of a committed-but-unclassified external call.\n\n**6. Terminals — PASS**\n`nodes/terminal.py:48-108` defines exactly the 6 terminal kinds (UNIT_ACCEPTED, COMPLETE, INTERRUPTED, PAUSED_PREREQUISITE, CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED, SYSTEM_FAILURE) in `TERMINAL_GUARDS`. `write_terminal` (`terminal.py:472-500`) independently re-derives every candidate via `validate_terminal_candidate` and downgrades any unsupported claim to `SYSTEM_FAILURE` (`terminal.py:446-469`), never trusting the proposing guard. `_validate_paused` (`terminal.py:307-327`) explicitly rejects a PAUSED_PREREQUISITE candidate if `pending_failure.class != \"pause\"` — so tool/transport/schema/render/integrity/implementation faults (which carry a different failure class) cannot masquerade as a genuine external prerequisite pause.\n\n**7. CLI — PASS**\n`runtime/run_curriculum.py:527-586` (`_run_live`) is the single live path; both fresh (`_prepare_fresh`) and resume (`_prepare_resume`) branches call `build_curriculum_factory_graph` (imported at line 42) exactly once each, then `compiled.invoke(...)` (line 470). No references to \"simulation\", \"session_bridge\", or \"Plan25/plan-25\" exist anywhere in `run_curriculum.py` or `graph.py` (grep returned no matches). The module's own docstring (lines 1-25) explicitly disclaims holding any node body/guard/join/acceptance rule itself.\n\nNo FINDINGS to report — all 7 items PASS based on direct code inspection."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":71533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":340,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019kwJZYNZqUFLgLkAmjUyqq","session_id":"47f42b4a-0f2f-488f-942b-22d2e1825427","uuid":"f358f057-b5b2-4696-8502-38c9b10a526f","timestamp":"2026-08-13T00:23:15.625Z","request_id":"req_011CdynzmHk4UoAMfXYcswVs","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Verify eight-job and invariant evidence"}
