_FAILURE) in `TERMINAL_GUARDS`. `write_terminal` (`terminal.py:472-500`) independently re-derives every candidate via `validate_terminal_candidate` and downgrades any unsupported claim to `SYSTEM_FAILURE` (`terminal.py:446-469`), never trusting the proposing guard. `_validate_paused` (`terminal.py:307-327`) explicitly rejects a PAUSED_PREREQUISITE candidate if `pending_failure.class != \"pause\"` — so tool/transport/schema/render/integrity/implementation faults (which carry a different failure class) cannot masquerade as a genuine external prerequisite pause.\n\n**7. CLI — PASS**\n`runtime/run_curriculum.py:527-586` (`_run_live`) is the single live path; both fresh (`_prepare_fresh`) and resume (`_prepare_resume`) branches call `build_curriculum_factory_graph` (imported at line 42) exactly once each, then `compiled.invoke(...)` (line 470). No references to \"simulation\", \"session_bridge\", or \"Plan25/plan-25\" exist anywhere in `run_curriculum.py` or `graph.py` (grep returned no matches). The module's own docstring (lines 1-25) explicitly disclaims holding any node body/guard/join/acceptance rule itself.\n\nNo FINDINGS to report — all 7 items PASS based on direct code inspection.","usage":{"total_tokens":72113,"tool_uses":34,"duration_ms":89209},"uuid":"5085c7ae-d8a3-401a-9c49-b8b5d3debf9f","session_id":"47f42b4a-0f2f-488f-942b-22d2e1825427"}
